report.suggested_fix:
Add a defensive null-check or fallback to an empty dictionary when accessing user preferences in get_user_notification_preference:

```python
def get_user_notification_preference(user_id: str, channel: str) -> bool:
    """Check if a user has opted in for a specific notification channel."""
    user = get_user(user_id)
    if not user:
        return False
    preferences = user.get("preferences")
    if preferences is None:
        return True  # Or False depending on default preference policy
    return bool(preferences.get(channel, True))
```
